source code as you receive it, in any medium, provided that you
conspicuously and appropriately publish on each copy an appropriate
copyright notice; keep intact all notices stating that this License
and any non-permissive terms added in accord with section 7 apply to
the code; keep intact all notices of the absence of any warranty; and
give all recipients a copy of this License along with the Program.

  4. Conveying Modified Source Versions.

  You may convey a work based on the Program, or the modifications to
produce it from the Program, in the form of source code under the terms
of section 3, provided that you also meet all of these conditions:

    a) The work must carry prominent notices stating that you modified
    it, and giving a relevant date.

    b) The work must carry prominent notices stating that it is
    released under this License and any conditions added under section 7.

    c) You must license the entire work, as a whole, under this
    License to anyone who comes into possession of a copy.

    d) If the work has interactive user interfaces, each must display
